 "recap": [
  "Tagalog has 14 question words: síno, anó, alín, gaáno, paáno, bakit, kailán, nasaán, saán, ilán, magkáno, kaníno, para sa kaníno, sa kaníno.",
  "Gaáno asks about degree; paáno about a process. Nasaán asks where a person or thing is; saán where an action happens.",
  "Kaníno (whose) is answered with a possessive pronoun such as ákin, kaniyá or kanilá.",
  "Plural question words are doubled: alín-alín, kaní-kanino, anu-anó. Nasaán and bakit are never doubled.",
  "Iyán and itó shorten to 'yan and 'to: Síno 'yan? Kaníno 'to? Anó 'yan?"
 ]
}